{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile","title":"lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.md","line":44,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.tex#lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:constant-curvature-tensor]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:geodesic]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:parallel-frame]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.tex","label":"lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile","line":62,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Constant-curvature normal Jacobi profile]\n\\label{lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile}\n\\uses{lem:constant-curvature-tensor,def:geodesic,lem:parallel-frame}\n\n\nFor every $K\\in\\mathbb R$ there are functions $s,s'$ satisfying\n$s''+Ks=0$, $s(0)=0$, and $s'(0)=1$.  Along a unit-speed geodesic\nin constant curvature $K$, if $E$ is parallel and perpendicular to\nthe velocity, then $J=sE$ is a Jacobi field with covariant derivative\n$\\nabla J=s'E$.\n\\end{lemma}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Constant-curvature normal Jacobi profile] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a636f6e7374616e742d6375727661747572652d6e6f726d616c2d6a61636f62692d70726f66696c65\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23lem%3Aconstant-curvature-tensor\">↗ lem:constant-curvature-tensor</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Ageodesic\">↗ def:geodesic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23lem%3Aparallel-frame\">↗ lem:parallel-frame</a> <p></p>For every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K\\in \\mathbb R$\">$K\\in \\mathbb R$</span> there are functions <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s,s&#x27;$\">$s,s&#x27;$</span> satisfying <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s&#x27;&#x27;+Ks=0$\">$s&#x27;&#x27;+Ks=0$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s(0)=0$\">$s(0)=0$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s&#x27;(0)=1$\">$s&#x27;(0)=1$</span>. Along a unit-speed geodesic in constant curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$K$\">$K$</span>, if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E$\">$E$</span> is parallel and perpendicular to the velocity, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J=sE$\">$J=sE$</span> is a Jacobi field with covariant derivative <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla J=s&#x27;E$\">$\\nabla J=s&#x27;E$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-curvature-exp-nonsingular-nonzero","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:constant-curvature-tensor","title":"lem:constant-curvature-tensor","label":"lem:constant-curvature-tensor"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:geodesic","title":"def:geodesic","label":"def:geodesic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:parallel-frame","title":"lem:parallel-frame","label":"lem:parallel-frame"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-curvature-exp-nonsingular-nonzero","title":"lem:constant-curvature-exp-nonsingular-nonzero","label":"lem:constant-curvature-exp-nonsingular-nonzero"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile","title":"lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Constant-curvature normal Jacobi profile]\n\\label{lem:constant-curvature-normal-jacobi-profile}\n\\uses{lem:constant-curvature-tensor,def:geodesic,lem:parallel-frame}\n\n\nFor every $K\\in\\mathbb R$ there are functions $s,s'$ satisfying\n$s''+Ks=0$, $s(0)=0$, and $s'(0)=1$.  Along a unit-speed geodesic\nin constant curvature $K$, if $E$ is parallel and perpendicular to\nthe velocity, then $J=sE$ is a Jacobi field with covariant derivative\n$\\nabla J=s'E$.\n\\end{lemma}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:constant-curvature-tensor","title":"lem:constant-curvature-tensor","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:geodesic","title":"def:geodesic","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:parallel-frame","title":"lem:parallel-frame","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}